    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our clear focal point. Boasting an elite score of 79.089, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** thrives in today\u2019s matchup against Pallante; his high-efficiency profile is bolstered by a favorable platoon edge (+14%) and, crucially, a slow pitcher delivery profile that drastically increases his stolen base upside\u2014a priority given our mandate to target speed. **Caleb Durbin** also projects as a strong play (65.77) against Mason Barnett. While we are awaiting official confirmation on his #5 spot, his combination of a hitter-friendly park (+10%) and an exploitable SP xERA of 4.47 makes him a cornerstone of the middle infield today.\n\nElsewhere, the lineup relies on calculated platoon advantages to scrape together value. **Lars Nootbaar** (59.86) is a high-upside play against Assad, benefiting from an 11% platoon boost, while **Junior Caminero** (55.92) remains a start despite facing a tougher arm in Winn, C. Conversely, **Chase Meidroth** (44.94) and **Carson Benge** (51.51) occupy the marginal tier of our starting nine. **Carson Benge** warrants a specific \u26a0\ufe0f flag due to a 35% rain risk, which could shorten his outing or force a late-inning replacement. We are currently resting our heavy hitters\u2014**Yordan Alvarez**, **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Christian Yelich**\u2014as all four are inactive today, leaving our depth pieces like **Hyeseong Kim**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Colt Keith** on the bench to preserve our limited game caps for more favorable matchups later in the week.",
